00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:08.070 align:start position:0%
european ministers have called on  switzerland to honour its eu obligations  to respect the free movement of citizens  following a referendum in the country  over the weekend  the vote saw a slim majority of people  support immigration quotas  and while switzerland is not an eu  member it has signed agreements that  committed  not to hinder cross-border circulation  the council of the european union  respects the internal democratic  procedure of switzerland  and the outcome of the referendum  on the other hand the council expects  that the swiss federation confederation  will honor its obligation arising  from its agreements and treaties with  the european union  in other developments the general  affairs council could not reach a  qualified majority vote  against the introduction of a  genetically modified type of maze  under procedural arrangements the  decision now falls to the european  commission  the ministers also paved the way for a  summit of eu leaders in march  which will put the spotlight on climate  change energy and the economy  the leaders are set to debate a proposed  framework for energy for the 2020-2030  period  and to examine how much has been done to  implement energy recommendations they  handed down in may
 

